={
  "populationLong": "This will be a retrospective chart review of clinical outcomes from a single glaucoma surgeon at one site. Approximately 51 adult patients with mild to moderate primary open angle glaucoma who were on topical glaucoma medications and have undergone cataract extraction with OMNI canaloplasty plus successful Hydrus implantation or cataract extraction with OMNI canaloplasty alone will be included. The planned sample size of 51 patients, with 34 in the Hydrus plus OMNI group and 17 in the OMNI alone group, is based on available data and is considered sufficient to detect a meaningful difference in medication reduction while allowing for potential missing data. Only subjects who meet all inclusion criteria and do not meet any exclusion criteria, and for whom appropriate informed consent and regulatory approvals have been obtained, will be included in the analysis.",
  "inclusionCriteria": "• Adult patients with mild-to-moderate primary open angle glaucoma who were on topical glaucoma medications and have undergone cataract extraction with OMNI canaloplasty plus successful Hydrus implantation or cataract extraction with OMNI canaloplasty alone.",
  "exclusionCriteria": "• Patients with angle closure glaucoma or secondary forms of glaucoma due to neovascularization of the angle, uveitic glaucoma, congenital glaucoma, or glaucoma due to congenital anomalies.\n• Patients with abnormal anterior segment examination other than cataract will be excluded from the study, including patients with pigment dispersion and pseudoexfoliation.\n• Patients with refractory CME or CME persisting 3 months or more post operatively.\n• Patients with incomplete IOP, medication logs or VF data within the 2 year post operative period."
}

